I knew At least, from a Korean standpoint, what it gets used for.

19
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:08,000
But yeah, it does happen.

20
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:14,790
So what is the best description for Kimchi to people in here?

21
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:21,570
I'd say it's fermented cabbage. Korean fermented cabbage.

22
00:01:23,730 --> 00:01:31,930
where I worked, I got introduced to a restaurant, a Kimchi Jjigae restaurant, by my coworkers,

23
00:01:31,930 --> 00:01:35,610
and we used to go there all the time.

24
00:01:35,610 --> 00:01:41,530
Like, we probably as a group would go there once a week, every other week or so,

25
00:01:41,530 --> 00:01:48,420
but if there was ever times where I really wanted it, and no one could go with me, I went by myself,

26
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:52,990
because it was just... In the buildings right next to where we worked,

27
00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:57,100
so it was very close and easy to get to.

28
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:00,550
So the people who worked there obviously knew us very well.

29
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:02,890
Especially when I would go by myself.

30
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:06,970
I mean, all of us as a group of foreigners kind of got stared at.

31
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:11,100
But when I'd go by myself, people were really shocked.

32
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:18,720
So I had my meal paid for at least two times, I think, while I was there.

33
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:22,510
Because they were always different Koreans, usually older,

34
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:28,570
and they'd come in and then be shocked to see a foreigner sitting down to eat Kimchi jjigae.

35
00:02:28,570 --> 00:02:33,860
So yeah, so I had my meal paid for. They bought it at least two times, I think.

36
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:37,520
Kelly.

37
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:42,010
Did you expect that you'd have Kimchi jjigae this often in the USA?

38
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:43,970
No, I did not.

39
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:50,810
But I feel like I kind of encouraged it by giving you a 10 out of 10 on that one soup you made.

40
00:02:50,810 --> 00:02:58,690
And unfortunately, some of them have been good, but none of them have quite lived up to that one you made.

41
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:09,060
I was introduced to the Kimchi Jjigae restaurant by my coworkers.

42
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:15,480
And I can't say like really why it was so good, but I just know that I really liked it,

43
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:18,340
and we went all the time.

44
00:03:18,340 --> 00:03:21,950
And it basically made it where, to me,

45
00:03:21,950 --> 00:03:24,540
that style of kimchi jjigae

46
